{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1091","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1091","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1091\",\"parent_revision\":\"b513ad574d352704a35d749a886c15f6fc1dd2ce\",\"root_revision\":\"95c8da8342ed49999d5b4960f6de974c89b37bea21d77f4281aba3f0c8a11a3e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe SAM dispatch loop in implement-feature spawns a fresh agent for every task, even when previously spawned teammates of the same type are idle with context headroom remaining. Each fresh spawn re-loads architecture specs, codebase patterns, and domain context that an idle teammate already holds in its window \u2014 incurring the full context-acquisition cost again on shared-prefix work.\\n\\nWhen consecutive tasks share the same knowledge domain (e.g., multiple python-cli-architect tasks on the same module), an idle teammate that completed T01 already knows the function signatures, import conventions, and local patterns needed for T02 and T03. Routing the next task to that teammate via SendMessage amortizes the prompt-load cost across tasks. A new cold-start agent must re-derive all of it.\\n\\nThe current model treats \\\"one task = one agent\\\" as the unit of work. The more efficient unit is \\\"one shared-context cluster = one agent session\\\" \u2014 reusing a session as long as context headroom and domain overlap hold, and spawning fresh only when the domain shifts or the window is under pressure.\\n\\nThis applies to both the implementation dispatch loop (implement-feature) and the quality gate dispatch loop (complete-implementation). The break-even point between reuse and fresh spawn depends on shared-prefix size, context growth rate, and per-task output volume.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-28T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **reuse idle same-domain teammates in sam dispatch loop while context headroom is available** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-28T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request + session write-up 2026-03-28\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-28)\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- #1092 Expose teammate context headroom \u2014 dispatch loop cannot evaluate the reuse condition without this signal\\n\",\"digest\":\"a8f52054782a5061d242b030c0a792c225aff317d77d3fbf03b7deae2dac69c3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg6TEg\"}"}